Midnight  came.  Planes  flew.  Banks  opened.  And  then  came  the
strange part: because so little happened, a chorus concluded nothing
would have happened, that the whole effort was hysteria. Some coun-
tries  that  spent  little  also  passed  quietly,  so  the  true  size  of  the
disaster that was avoided is still argued about. But that vast act of
anticipatory engineering is remembered, by many, as an overreac-
tion.  And  one  caution  runs  the  other  way:  a  missed  AI  forecast
doesnʼt get to call itself a disaster averted. Y2K had a known deadline
